IMPORT prelude

-- Statistics Act 1973 (Singapore) -- the statistical requisition and the duty to answer it (ss 2, 5, First Schedule), the
-- Chief Statistician's directions to public agencies (s 6), the secrecy rule and its exceptions (s 7, Third Schedule),
-- impersonation (s 8), the requisition offences and their penalties (s 9), composition (s 10) and service (s 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SA1973.txt. The
-- deposit says it incorporates "all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest annotation seen in it is
-- S 439/2026 (wef 30/06/2026) to the Second Schedule. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is numbered one
-- ahead of the body; this encoding follows the BODY's section numbers.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a person, business or
-- public agency actually meets: being served with a requisition, having to answer it, the limits on what must be answered,
-- the offences and penalties, who may see the answers. Not encoded: the national statistical coordinator's duties and the
-- refusal procedure for research and statistics units (s 4), the s 6(4) immunities, the certificate as prima facie evidence
-- (s 9(2)), the rule-making power (s 12) and any rules made under it (none retrieved), and amendment of the Schedules (s 13).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Statistics Act 1973 -- requisitions`

§§ `2, 5 and First Schedule -- a requisition, and who must answer it`

-- s 2: "statistical purposes" means "the compilation of statistics or the preparation of anonymised microdata relating to
-- any subject matter listed in the First Schedule". The First Schedule lists 55 subject matters, among them "Income and
-- expenditure", "Prices and charges", "Tourism", "Crime", "Births and deaths" and "Housing".
-- s 5(1): "The Chief Statistician or the director of a research and statistics unit may issue a requisition to any person or
-- the occupier of any premises ... for the purpose of obtaining data for statistical purposes, and every such person or
-- occupier is bound to furnish the particulars and supply the information to the best of the person's or occupier's
-- knowledge and belief."
-- s 5(2): a requisition must (a) be in writing; (b) be served in the manner specified in s 11; and (c) specify the
-- particulars or information required.
DECLARE Issuer IS ONE OF
    `the Chief Statistician`
    `the director of a research and statistics unit`
    `a ministry division not listed in the Second Schedule`
    `a private market research firm`

DECLARE Subject IS ONE OF
    `income and expenditure`
    `prices and charges`
    `tourism`
    `crime`
    `births and deaths`
    `housing`
    `a subject not listed in the First Schedule`

DECLARE Requisition HAS
    `issued by` IS AN Issuer
    `about` IS A Subject
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `served under section 11` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the particulars required` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the subject` IS A Subject
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subject is a statistical purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the subject`
    WHEN `a subject not listed in the First Schedule` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the issuer` IS AN Issuer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issuer may requisition` IF
    CONSIDER `the issuer`
    WHEN `the Chief Statistician` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the director of a research and statistics unit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the requisition` IS A Requisition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requisition is valid` IF
        `the issuer may requisition` (`the requisition`'s `issued by`)
    AND `the subject is a statistical purpose` (`the requisition`'s `about`)
    AND `the requisition`'s `in writing`
    AND `the requisition`'s `served under section 11`
    AND `the requisition`'s `specifies the particulars required`

-- s 5(4): "No person is bound to furnish any particulars or information other than those which are accessible to the person
-- or derived by the person from any business, occupation or work in the conduct or supervision of which the person is
-- engaged."
GIVEN `the requisition` IS A Requisition, `accessible to the person` IS A BOOLEAN, `derived from the person's own business or work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is bound to furnish the item` IF
        `the requisition is valid` `the requisition`
    AND (`accessible to the person` OR `derived from the person's own business or work`)

§§ `6 -- directions to public agencies`

-- s 6(1): the Chief Statistician may "in writing direct" (a) the director of a research and statistics unit to supply what it
-- obtained under a requisition, or (b) any public agency to supply what it holds, whether or not the agency or its data source
-- "is under any obligation (whether imposed by any written law or otherwise) not to disclose".
-- s 6(2): "Despite the provisions of this Act or any other written law" they must furnish it, except, for a (1)(b) direction,
-- anything exempted by (a) the Minister responsible for the agency or (b) the Minister responsible for the data source.
-- s 6(5): "Subsection (1) does not apply to any particulars or information obtained under any written law administered by the
-- Monetary Authority of Singapore."
GIVEN `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `addressed to a research and statistics unit director` IS A BOOLEAN, `obtained under a law the Monetary Authority administers` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by the agency's Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by the data source's Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `the agency owes a duty of confidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient must comply with the direction` IF
        `the direction is in writing`
    AND (NOT `obtained under a law the Monetary Authority administers`)
    AND (    `addressed to a research and statistics unit director`
         OR  ((NOT `exempted by the agency's Minister`) AND (NOT `exempted by the data source's Minister`)))

§§ `7 and Third Schedule -- secrecy`

-- s 7(1): "A person must not disclose any particulars or information obtained under section 5 or 6 in a form that may identify
-- any person without the prior consent in writing of the person that may be identified by the disclosure."
-- s 7(2): "Despite subsection (1), the Chief Statistician or the director of a research and statistics unit ... may disclose"
-- (a) statistics which do not identify any person; (b) anonymised microdata to (i) any public agency or (ii) a person within a
-- class in the Third Schedule; (c) for proceedings for an offence under this Act; (d) information "of a general nature relating
-- to the products or services provided by, the number of employees in or the addresses of, an establishment"; (e) information
-- "already available in the public domain".
-- Third Schedule: (1) "Any consultant commissioned by a public agency"; (2) an employee of a specified university (or a person
-- assisting one) to whom disclosure for research "is supported by the specified university".
-- s 7(4): disclosure contrary to the section, or failure to comply with conditions imposed under s 7(3), is an offence.
--
-- INFERENCE: anonymised microdata is treated here as a form that "may identify" a person, so that s 7(1) catches it unless an
-- exception applies. The text does not say so; but s 7(2)(b) would be pointless if microdata fell outside s 7(1).
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `a public agency`
    `a consultant commissioned by a public agency`
    `a university researcher whose research the university supports`
    `a private company`
    `a newspaper`

DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `obtained under section 5 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made by the Chief Statistician or a director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to` IS A Recipient
    `may identify a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as anonymised microdata` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prior written consent of the person identified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for proceedings for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `general information about an establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `already in the public domain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breaches a condition imposed under section 7(3)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient may receive anonymised microdata` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a public agency` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a consultant commissioned by a public agency` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a university researcher whose research the university supports` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7(1) catches the disclosure` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `obtained under section 5 or 6`
    AND (`the disclosure`'s `may identify a person` OR `the disclosure`'s `as anonymised microdata`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `prior written consent of the person identified`)

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 7(2) exception applies` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `made by the Chief Statistician or a director`
    AND (    (`the disclosure`'s `as anonymised microdata` AND `the recipient may receive anonymised microdata` (`the disclosure`'s `to`))
         OR  `the disclosure`'s `for proceedings for an offence under this Act`
         OR  `the disclosure`'s `general information about an establishment`
         OR  `the disclosure`'s `already in the public domain`)

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `breaches a condition imposed under section 7(3)`
    OR  (`section 7(1) catches the disclosure` `the disclosure` AND (NOT `a section 7(2) exception applies` `the disclosure`))

§§ `9 -- failing to answer a requisition`

-- s 9(1)(a): a person who "wilfully refuses or without lawful excuse (the burden of proof of which lies on the person) neglects
-- to furnish the particulars or information required by a requisition within the time allowed", or in the specified form or
-- place; (b) "wilfully furnishes ... any false particulars"; (c) "refuses to answer, or wilfully gives a false answer to, any
-- question necessary for obtaining" them.
-- The lawful-excuse words attach to neglect, not to wilful refusal.
-- INFERENCE: particulars outside s 5(4) are not "required by a requisition", so failing to give them is no offence.
GIVEN `bound to furnish` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `neglected` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully gave false particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 9(1) offence is committed` IF
        `bound to furnish`
    AND (    `wilfully refused`
         OR  (`neglected` AND (NOT `proved a lawful excuse`))
         OR  `wilfully gave false particulars`)

§§ `7(4), 8, 9 and 10 -- penalties and composition`

-- s 7(4): "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- s 8(1): "A person who impersonates a statistical officer ... shall be liable on conviction to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 6 months." No fine is provided.
-- s 9(1): "a fine not exceeding $1,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $100 for every
-- day during which the offence continues after conviction." No imprisonment is provided.
-- s 10: the Chief Statistician or a director "may compound any of the offences under section 9(1) by accepting ... a sum not
-- exceeding $200."
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to answer a requisition`
    `giving false particulars`
    `unlawful disclosure`
    `impersonating a statistical officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is under section 9(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to answer a requisition` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `giving false particulars` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the offence is under section 9(1)` `the offence`
    THEN 1000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days continued after conviction`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `unlawful disclosure` THEN 10000
         OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlawful disclosure` THEN 12
    WHEN `impersonating a statistical officer` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the sum offered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
        `the offence is under section 9(1)` `the offence`
    AND `the sum offered` AT MOST 200

§§ `11 -- service of a requisition`

-- s 11(1)(a), individual: personal delivery; leaving with an adult apparently resident or employed at, or prepaid registered
-- post to, the residence or place of business; or "affixing a copy ... in a conspicuous place" at that address. No fax.
-- (b) partnership, and (c) body corporate or LLP: delivery to a partner, secretary or similar officer (or LLP manager); leaving
-- at or registered post to the place of business or registered office in Singapore; or fax to the number operated there. No
-- affixing.
-- (2) occupier: delivery to an adult on the premises or, "if there is no such person on the premises to whom it can with
-- reasonable diligence be delivered, by affixing the requisition to a conspicuous part of the premises".
-- (4) any of them: if the person "has an agent within Singapore, the requisition may be delivered to the agent".
-- s 11(1) is "Subject to any rules made under section 12"; none were retrieved.
DECLARE Addressee IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a partnership`
    `a company`
    `the occupier of premises`

DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `personal delivery`
    `leaving it at the address`
    `prepaid registered post`
    `fax`
    `affixing it at the address`
    `delivery to an agent in Singapore`

GIVEN `the addressee` IS AN Addressee, `the method` IS A Method, `an adult could be found on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the method is good service` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `delivery to an agent in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `personal delivery` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `leaving it at the address` THEN NOT (`the addressee` EQUALS `the occupier of premises`)
    WHEN `prepaid registered post` THEN NOT (`the addressee` EQUALS `the occupier of premises`)
    WHEN `fax` THEN (`the addressee` EQUALS `a partnership`) OR (`the addressee` EQUALS `a company`)
    OTHERWISE (`the addressee` EQUALS `an individual`) OR ((`the addressee` EQUALS `the occupier of premises`) AND (NOT `an adult could be found on the premises`))
